{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dispiteous-copacetic-goldfinch","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Suspected sibling of 7dea-2f00-db57-4a96 (completion-cache shared-tmp collision)\n\n`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py::save_checkpoint` writes `tmp = d / f\".tmp-{envelope.digest}.json\"` then `tmp.replace(path)`, where `_checkpoint_dir` is `.rebar/cache/plan-review/<ticket_id>` — keyed by ticket only, NOT run-scoped. Two concurrent plan-review workers saving a checkpoint for the SAME (ticket, digest) therefore target the SAME temp file: both write it, both call `tmp.replace(path)`, and the second raises `FileNotFoundError` (the first replace consumed the temp), which the outer `except Exception: return False` swallows — a silently lost checkpoint. This is the exact construct proven in 7dea (shared deterministic temp name + concurrent writers), in a different subsystem.\n\n## Mandatory reproduction before remediation\nMirror 7dea's experiment: drive two concurrent save_checkpoint writers for the same ticket+digest with a barrier forcing both temp writes before either replace; capture each writer's return value, suppressed exceptions, final JSON validity, and orphaned temp files. Include a cross-process case.\n\n## Remediation if reproduced\nSame fix shape as 7dea: unique same-directory temp via a stdlib tempfile primitive (tempfile.mkstemp(dir=d, ...)), retain atomic replace onto the shared final <digest>.json, and bounded cleanup of only the writer's own temp on failure. No contract/output change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A deterministic two-writer experiment proves or falsifies the collision (thread + cross-process).\n- [ ] If reproduced, a RED regression test fails against the shared .tmp-<digest>.json implementation before the fix.\n- [ ] If reproduced, writers use unique same-directory temp paths and atomically replace the shared final key; concurrent stress leaves one valid record, no partial, no residue.\n- [ ] If falsified, no production change; close with the falsifying evidence.","id":"d284-0454-596a-46c1","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["concurrency","cache","plan-review","experiment-first"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"plan-review save_checkpoint shares a .tmp-<digest>.json path across concurrent same-ticket writers"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787943543727010001,"uuid":"8442e4ef-83b4-4802-ad86-70498a68dcd9"}